# UI Design System

## Style Direction
**Modern & clean** — minimal, generous whitespace, calm neutral palette with one warm accent color. Feels trustworthy and welcoming for a religious community app.

## Mobile-First (Required)
Always write Tailwind classes mobile-first and layer up:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — desktop-first
<div className="grid-cols-3 sm:grid-cols-1">

// ✅ GOOD — mobile-first
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
```

- Base styles target small screens (≤ 640px)
- Use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` to progressively enhance for larger screens
- Test layouts at 375px width as the baseline

## Touch Targets
All interactive elements must be comfortably tappable:

```tsx
// ✅ Minimum touch target
<button className="min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px] px-4 py-3">
  Entrar
</button>
```

- Minimum 44×44px for buttons, links, and icons
- Add sufficient padding — never rely on text alone as the tap area
- No hover-only interactions; all states must work on touch

## Layout Patterns

```tsx
// Page wrapper
<main className="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-6">

// Card
<div className="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">

// Section heading
<h2 className="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900">Próximos Eventos</h2>
```

## Typography
- Headings: `font-semibold` or `font-bold`, `text-neutral-900`
- Body: `text-neutral-700`, `text-base` or `text-sm`
- Muted / secondary: `text-neutral-500`
- Line height: prefer `leading-relaxed` for body text

## Color Palette (Tailwind)
| Role | Class |
|---|---|
| Primary accent | `blue-700` / `blue-600` (or a warm gold once brand is defined) |
| Background | `neutral-50` or `white` |
| Surface (cards) | `white` with `border-neutral-200` |
| Text primary | `neutral-900` |
| Text secondary | `neutral-500` |
| Destructive | `red-600` |
| Success | `green-600` |

## Navigation on Mobile
- Use a **bottom navigation bar** on mobile for primary routes
- Top navbar reserved for page title + secondary actions (back, settings)

## Accessibility
- Always include `aria-label` on icon-only buttons
- Use semantic HTML: `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<header>`, `<section>`, `<article>`
- Ensure sufficient color contrast (WCAG AA minimum)
